        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-184",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "INCOMPLETE DENY-LIST \u2014 `builtins.__import__` is not blocked. The `_unsafe_globals` entries for `\"builtins\"` and `\"__builtin__\"` are the exact set {\"eval\", \"compile\", \"getattr\", \"apply\", \"exec\", \"open\", \"breakpoint\"}. `__import__` is absent, as are `setattr`, `delattr`, `globals`, `vars`, `input`, `help` and `memoryview`. Because the module key `builtins` IS present in `_unsafe_globals`, `unsafe_filter` is non-None but `\"__import__\" not in unsafe_filter`, so the parent-module \"*\" propagation never applies and control reaches the `else` branch \u2192 `SafetyLevel.Suspicious`, issues_count unchanged, CLI exit 0. A pickle containing `GLOBAL builtins __import__` (the canonical pickle RCE import primitive) is therefore reported as non-infected. Note `builtins.help` is a further gap because the `pydoc` module itself IS deny-listed with \"*\", so the alias reaches deny-listed functionality under a non-deny-listed name.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Re-derived from source. The deny-list entries for \"__builtin__\" (scanner.py:101-110) and \"builtins\" (scanner.py:111-120) are exactly {eval, compile, getattr, apply, exec, open, breakpoint}; __import__, setattr, delattr, globals, vars, input, help and memoryview are all absent, while \"pydoc\": \"*\" at line 169 blocks pydoc at module level. Because the \"builtins\" key IS present, unsafe_filter is non-None at scanner.py:368, so the parent-module \"*\" propagation at 371-377 (gated on `unsafe_filter is None and \".\" in g.module`) can never fire; the name test at 383 fails, safe_filter is None (no \"builtins\" key in _safe_globals, 66-98), and control reaches the else at 390 -> SafetyLevel.Suspicious with issues_count unchanged, hence infected_files=0 (393) and CLI exit 0 (cli.py:76). The repo's own tests codify this (test_scanner.py:390,394,490 assert Global(\"builtins\",\"__import__\", SafetyLevel.Suspicious)). Reachability is sound: _build_scan_result_from_raw_globals has reachable_from_entry=true, hop_distance=0. CORRECTIONS to the analyst: (1) the defect spans lines 100-120, not 100-100; (2) the \"canonical pickle RCE primitive goes undetected\" framing is overstated -- __import__ alone only yields a module object, and the chaining primitives needed to reach execution (getattr, operator/_operator attrgetter/itemgetter/methodcaller) ARE deny-listed; the two in-repo GHSA fixtures whose first global is builtins __import__ (tests/data2/GHSA-46h3-79wf-xr6c.pkl, GHSA-955r-x9j8-7rhh.pkl) are still flagged Dangerous via their _operator globals (test_scanner.py:388-395). The stronger gap is builtins.help, unblocked while pydoc is blocked with \"*\" and commented as dangerous for pydoc.pipepager -- a non-deny-listed name aliasing explicitly deny-listed functionality. Confirmed as an incomplete-deny-list / detection-gap defect (CWE-184), severity MEDIUM rather than HIGH since no end-to-end bypass using only non-deny-listed globals was established and the global is still surfaced as Suspicious. Exploit-reference check not applicable: first-party code, no pinned component version, and the Metasploit corpus returned \"exploit corpus unavailable: not indexed\", so I claim neither exploitable-by-module nor patched."
          },
